<title>FRANCE: EU authorises free-mkt, intervention grain sales.</title>
<headline>EU authorises free-mkt, intervention grain sales.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, grain trade sources and member country officials said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  198,900		18.00 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		 95,500		31.50 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		    22,000		31.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		   20,500		32.80 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>The EU also sold the following amounts of grain from intervention stores.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Minimum price</p>
<p>German barley	 3,885		 97.87 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>German rye	   13,692		 103.33 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
